  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch14-02> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch14-02--gpt> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch14-02--gpt> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "GPT-5.6 Sol on thompson1917-ch14-02: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.86" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.861"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.9"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Intersection angles are directly measurable and sharply distinguish isogonal from orthogonal patterns. Large public image sources and straightforward image analysis make the prediction resolvable now." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Extract opposing parastichy families from calibrated sunflower images and measure their local intersection angles across each disc and among heads. Approximate constancy away from 90 degrees supports the claim; systematic angle variation or frequent orthogonality refutes it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Herbarium images may distort three-dimensional capitula.", "Parastichy tracing can be ambiguous near the disc center and edge." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch14-02--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch14-02--gpt--dataset-2> .
